  "summary": "STARTTLS response injection allows a man-in-the-middle to forge SMTP replies",
  "details": "A man-in-the-middle can append replies of their own to the cleartext reply to\n`STARTTLS`. The client takes them for the server's replies to the commands it\nthen sends over TLS, so the attacker can, for example, make a message that the\nserver rejected look accepted.\n\nOnly connections upgraded with `STARTTLS` are affected (`Tls::Required` and\n`Tls::Opportunistic`, as set up by `starttls_relay`). Implicit TLS\n(`Tls::Wrapper`, as set up by `relay`) is not.",
  "severity": [
    {
      "type": "CVSS_V3",
      "score": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:L"
    }
  ],
